      "message": "[collect()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/slice/struct.Split.html#method.collect) doesn\u0027t work here because it can\u0027t add spaces (separator) between tokens.\n\n[intersperse()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/slice/struct.Split.html#method.intersperse) is the alternative in the iterator, but it\u0027s currently nightly-only experimental API.\n\nSo two alteratives are,\n- Use slice\u0027s [join()](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.slice.html#method.join)\n- Use itertool\u0027s [intersperse](https://docs.rs/itertools/latest/itertools/fn.intersperse.html)\n\n.. and using `join()` with `vector` seemed to be the cleaner way for me.",
